{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MUTATION LEDGER — all five items rewritten and mutation-verified. Gerrit change 1233\n(https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1233). Every mutation below was applied to\nPRODUCTION code (or, where noted, to the shared test-module predicate under test), never to the\nfixture, and each was reverted immediately after capturing the RED.\n\nITEM 1 — PAT never in repr(transport).\nMUTATED: added __repr__ to JiraDataCenterTransport returning\n\"<JiraDataCenterTransport project={self.project!r} client={self._client!r}>\";\nFAILED: test_the_pat_never_appears_in_the_repr_of_the_transport\nRED: AssertionError: the PAT reached a log-facing rendering of the transport via repr():\n\"<JiraDataCenterTransport project='DC' client=<Client token_auth='pat-xyz'>>\".\nThe test now builds the transport around _CredentialCarryingClient, which HOLDS the PAT and prints\nit in its own repr, self-checks that the fixture actually carries the credential, and asserts both\nrepr(t) and f\"{t}\" stay clean. vars(t) was deliberately NOT asserted: the client is an attribute, so\nvars() reprs it by construction and no transport can prevent that.\n\nITEM 2 — pagination structural guard teeth.\n_search_issues_calls_taking_the_default() now takes `src: str | None = None` falling back to\n_TRANSPORT_SRC.read_text(); the real guard's call is unchanged (no argument). Exactly ONE predicate\nremains in the module — the inline AST walk is deleted, not duplicated. The teeth test feeds it a\nsynthetic source with one unpaginated call (line 3) and TWO paginated negative controls (maxResults\nline 6, max_results line 9) and asserts offenders == [\"line 3\"].\nMUTATED: predicate never appends (offenders.append -> pass);\nFAILED: test_the_structural_guard_fires_on_a_synthetic_unpaginated_caller\nRED: AssertionError: ... it reported [] / assert [] == ['line 3']\nMUTATED: accepted keyword set narrowed to {\"maxResults\"} (drop \"max_results\");\nFAILED: test_the_structural_guard_fires_on_a_synthetic_unpaginated_caller\nRED: ... it reported ['line 3', 'line 9'] / assert ['line 3', 'line 9'] == ['line 3']\nThe negative controls are what make the second mutation bite — asserting only the positive offender\nwould have stayed green.\n\nITEM 3 — validate_assignee_exists RETURN VALUE, both backends. NO BUG FILED: the pre-implementation\ntriage is confirmed on both sides. DC (transport.py) returns str(_user_attr(user,\"name\") or\nassignee) or raises AssigneeNotFoundError. CLOUD (adapters/jira/acli.py) was checked INDEPENDENTLY\nand its contract IS deliberately different as expected: it returns u.get(\"accountId\") from an exact\nmatch on emailAddress/accountId/displayName, or a unique normalized match, else raises\nAssigneeNotFoundError; it additionally raises ValueError when neither issue_key nor project_key is\nsupplied. Neither backend has a path returning a bool.\nThe DC test now CALLS the member (the old body was `assert hasattr(...)`, verbatim what the\nparametrized member-set test in the same file already asserts) against a client whose matching user\nrecord ALSO carries an accountId, and asserts the result == \"dcuser\", is a str and not a bool, and\nis not the accountId. A new sibling test pins the Cloud accountId return.\nMUTATED: DC `return str(_user_attr(user, \"name\") or assignee)` -> `return True`;\nFAILED: test_validate_assignee_exists_returns_the_dc_username\nRED: AssertionError: DC must resolve to the USERNAME that flows on as the identity; got True /\nassert True == 'dcuser'\nMUTATED: DC same return -> str(_user_attr(user, \"accountId\") or assignee) (accountId-shaped);\nFAILED: test_validate_assignee_exists_returns_the_dc_username\nRED: ... got '5b10a2844c20165700ede21g' / assert '5b10a2844c20165700ede21g' == 'dcuser'\nMUTATED: Cloud exact-match branch `acct = u.get(\"accountId\")` -> u.get(\"displayName\");\nFAILED: test_cloud_validate_assignee_exists_returns_the_account_id_not_the_username\nRED: AssertionError: Cloud must resolve to the accountId ...; got 'DC User' /\nassert 'DC User' == '5b10a2844c20165700ede21g'\n\nITEM 4 — the 429 enumerated-mutations sweep. total <= 1 is now total == 1, and the blanket\npytest.raises(Exception) (with its # noqa: B017 and its false \"the TYPE is asserted per-member\nbelow\" comment) is replaced by pytest.raises(BackendHTTPError) with an assertion of .code == 429 per\nmember. All ten members pass unchanged, which means every one of them genuinely reaches the client\nexactly once — the == 1 form is not merely stricter, it is satisfied.\nMUTATED: delete_issue_link raises ValueError PRE-FLIGHT (before _call_logged reaches the client);\nrun in three configurations to isolate which assertion bites:\n  * CONFIG A, the OLD form (raises(Exception) + total <= 1): 1 passed — GREEN, the defect reproduced\n  * CONFIG B, count teeth only (raises(Exception) + total == 1): FAILED\n    test_every_mutating_transport_member_still_fails_on_the_first_429\n    RED: AssertionError: delete_issue_link issued 0 client calls under a 429 — exactly one is the\n    contract ... ZERO means the member failed BEFORE reaching the client / assert 0 == 1\n  * CONFIG C, as committed: FAILED same test, RED: ValueError: MUTANT D: pre-flight failure, client\n    never reached (the type assertion catches it even earlier)\nMUTATED: retry.py translation drops the status (int(status) if isinstance(status,int) else 0 -> 0);\nFAILED: test_every_mutating_transport_member_still_fails_on_the_first_429\nRED: AssertionError: create_issue surfaced HTTP 0, not the 429 the client raised — the translation\nlost the status ... / assert 0 == 429 + where 0 = <HTTPError 0: 'HTTP 429'>.code\n\nITEM 5 — unknown backend. BROADENED, not renamed, so the AC's behavioural mutation applies. The test\nnow imports select_backend/register/_reset_registry_for_test, registers a throwaway sentinel factory\ninside the reset context, asserts select_backend resolves it (positive control, so the miss below is\na real miss and not a selector that raises on everything), then asserts the unknown key raises\nBackendRegistryError, that the error is not a KeyError instance, and that its message names BOTH the\nmissing key and the registered ones.\nMUTATED: pointed the negative case at the key that DOES resolve (\"known-backend-for-this-test\");\nFAILED: test_an_unknown_backend_raises_the_registry_error_not_key_error\nRED: Failed: DID NOT RAISE BackendRegistryError\n\nGATES. Module sizes (LOC before -> after, hard cap 800, none approached it):\ntest_jira_dc_transport_heldout.py 241 -> 303; test_dc_transport_pagination_heldout.py 206 -> 221;\ntest_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py 464 -> 533; test_dc_rate_limit_retry_heldout.py 340 ->\n347. No src/** file was modified in the change; every production mutation above was reverted and\n`git status` verified clean after each. Full tests/unit/rebar_reconciler: 1886 passed. ruff check +\nformat and mypy pass via the pre-commit gate. No isinstance() against a runtime-checkable Protocol\nwas introduced, so the 3.11-vs-3.12 getattr_static change cannot bite; presence is asserted with\nhasattr directly."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785711307251870001,"uuid":"9bff778c-2cc7-426c-95dd-5b222b75f1fe"}